From 9940e091c383f594314f6b4c54d3d0c23e32c2a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Puranam V G Tejaswi <puranam.tejaswi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:38:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] FROMLIST: firmware: qcom: scm: Add
 qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs_is_available()

The Adreno driver asks the secure world to initialize some GPU registers
through qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs(), and fails to power up the GPU if this
call fails.

Not every secure world implements this call. When it is missing, the
call fails in the same way as a real error, so the driver cannot tell
the two cases apart.

Add qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs_is_available(), similar to
qcom_scm_set_gpu_smmu_aperture_is_available(), so that the driver can
check whether the secure world supports the call before making it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Puranam V G Tejaswi <puranam.tejaswi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261118-adreno-scm-fallback-v1-1-e99cdbf3121d@oss.qualcomm.com
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261118-adreno-scm-fallback-v1-1-e99cdbf3121d@oss.qualcomm.com]
Signed-off-by: Lokesh Kumar <lok@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c       | 7 +++++++
 include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 8d21a03c15da3..e515465a5b0a7 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -1995,6 +1995,13 @@ int qcom_scm_lmh_dcvsh(u32 payload_fn, u32 payload_reg, u32 payload_val,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_lmh_dcvsh);
 
+bool qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs_is_available(void)
+{
+	return __qcom_scm_is_call_available(__scm->dev, QCOM_SCM_SVC_GPU,
+					    QCOM_SCM_SVC_GPU_INIT_REGS);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs_is_available);
+
 int qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs(u32 gpu_req)
 {
 	struct qcom_scm_desc desc = {
diff --git a/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h b/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
index e505e9b6f49e9..9284fa435f9b4 100644
--- a/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
+++ b/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
@@ -170,6 +170,7 @@ bool qcom_scm_lmh_dcvsh_available(void);
  */
 #define QCOM_SCM_GPU_TSENSE_EN_REQ BIT(3)
 
+bool qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs_is_available(void);
 int qcom_scm_gpu_init_regs(u32 gpu_req);
 
 int qcom_scm_shm_bridge_create(u64 pfn_and_ns_perm_flags,

From 7bd9a3a34cc624f01ace13df4abba74c10dbbbd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Puranam V G Tejaswi <puranam.tejaswi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:38:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] FROMLIST: dt-bindings: display/msm: gpu: Document the CX
 SMMU aperture region

The CX SMMU aperture is a register block in the GPU. It holds the
location of the GPU SMMU context banks that the CP uses for pagetable
switching.

On some GPUs the block lies outside the existing GPU register regions.
Add it as an optional aperture region, so the driver can program it on
platforms where the secure world does not.

Signed-off-by: Puranam V G Tejaswi <puranam.tejaswi@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261118-adreno-scm-fallback-v1-3-e99cdbf3121d@oss.qualcomm.com
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261118-adreno-scm-fallback-v1-3-e99cdbf3121d@oss.qualcomm.com]
Signed-off-by: Lokesh Kumar <lok@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
index d0f5cff3286ef..d5bb5865d54fb 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ properties:
 
   reg:
     minItems: 1
-    maxItems: 3
+    maxItems: 4
 
   reg-names:
